1
00:02:04,140 --> 00:02:07,950
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

2
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:13,640
A message has just arrived from
the castle, my Bey.

3
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:28,490
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

4
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:34,220
''If you don't give Kulacahisar back...

5
00:02:38,920 --> 00:02:41,140
... I will sentence Bayhoca to death.''

6
00:03:06,960 --> 00:03:08,040
Lena!

7
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:38,120
No. Please, no!

8
00:04:03,300 --> 00:04:04,920
Bayhoca.

9
00:04:05,620 --> 00:04:07,420
My Bayhoca.

10
00:04:11,580 --> 00:04:14,260
If I return without my nephew...

11
00:04:16,540 --> 00:04:18,800
... my horse and my beyhood robe...

12
00:04:21,040 --> 00:04:23,920
... shall become my coffin.

13
00:04:25,920 --> 00:04:27,460
If I...

14
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:30,840
... don't fulfill my promise...

15
00:04:32,980 --> 00:04:35,120
... the Tent of Ertuğrul Gazi...

16
00:04:36,840 --> 00:04:38,860
... shall be my graveyard.

17
00:06:13,220 --> 00:06:14,800
Careful! Ambush!

18
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:38,560
BEFORE

19
00:06:41,360 --> 00:06:42,980
Where are you taking me?

20
00:06:43,400 --> 00:06:46,800
Didn't anyone tell you that curiosity is a
bad thing?

21
00:06:48,240 --> 00:06:51,000
You should kill me while you can.

22
00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:53,620
I don't agree with you, young man.

23
00:06:54,420 --> 00:06:59,640
Your life is not enough. I want all
the Kayı Tent to beg for their lives.

24
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:02,280
You have no idea about your enemy, Nikola.

25
00:07:02,780 --> 00:07:05,820
Only for Allah, a Kayı Alp falls on his
knees.

26
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:08,140
You've started to talk non sense.

27
00:07:10,440 --> 00:07:13,180
Did you already get accustomed to beating?

28
00:07:14,440 --> 00:07:18,260
Send my regards to the Lord of
İznik, Alexander.

29
00:07:18,680 --> 00:07:21,840
I hope he likes my little present over
here.

30
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:23,960
I'm sure he will, Nikola.

31
00:07:24,020 --> 00:07:25,840
And you'll be rewarded too.

32
00:07:25,880 --> 00:07:27,440
This is the aim of my life.

33
00:07:27,640 --> 00:07:29,360
Pleasing your friends.

34
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:45,160
Alexander, be careful.

35
00:07:45,820 --> 00:07:48,780
I don't want to see you at the hands of
Turks again.

36
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:53,820
If I ever come across them, I will bring
the head of their Bey, Osman, to you.

37
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:59,700
If you meet my Bey again, know that your
head will leave your body.

38
00:08:01,740 --> 00:08:04,380
Shut his mouth and mount him on the horse.

39
00:08:07,620 --> 00:08:12,160
Just like his uncle, he talks non sense.

40
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:25,220
On your horses, soldiers!

41
00:09:30,680 --> 00:09:33,200
A message from our spy in İnegöl, my Bey.

42
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:44,300
We know what Nikola is about to do.

43
00:09:44,300 --> 00:09:47,130
He is going to send Bayhoca to the
Lord of İznik.

44
00:09:47,140 --> 00:09:48,500
Lord of İznik?

45
00:09:49,160 --> 00:09:51,280
What about sentencing him to death?

46
00:09:51,500 --> 00:09:53,760
He came up with a better plan I guess.

47
00:09:54,140 --> 00:09:55,700
It might be a trap.

48
00:09:58,040 --> 00:10:02,430
Ever since I came to this tent, our spy
has always been loyal to us.

49
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:04,920
Why should he lie now?

50
00:10:05,100 --> 00:10:07,960
Come on. We must hurry up.

51
00:10:08,860 --> 00:10:11,640
We have to save my son from those
heathens.

52
00:10:16,540 --> 00:10:17,520
Osman.

53
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:20,120
Brother?

54
00:10:20,880 --> 00:10:23,080
What happened to my anxious Osman?

55
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:26,300
What happened to my roaring brother?

56
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:29,000
What are we waiting for?

57
00:10:29,260 --> 00:10:31,380
We can't lose more time.

58
00:10:32,840 --> 00:10:34,860
Let's save my child.

59
00:10:35,660 --> 00:10:36,760
Your nephew.

60
00:10:36,880 --> 00:10:38,280
Let's go!

61
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:06,280
Allahu Akbar!

62
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:13,760
Please, have mercy.

63
00:11:14,700 --> 00:11:15,880
We are just slaves.

64
00:11:16,020 --> 00:11:17,180
Alps!

65
00:11:17,460 --> 00:11:19,700
-Check the carriages!
-I'm here, son.

66
00:11:20,620 --> 00:11:21,840
The carriages!

67
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:43,720
Brother.

68
00:11:45,820 --> 00:11:47,040
Brother?

69
00:11:54,500 --> 00:11:56,260
Alps!

70
00:11:57,060 --> 00:11:58,440
Attack!

71
00:12:30,380 --> 00:12:32,140
Feudal Landlord Nikola!

72
00:12:34,260 --> 00:12:37,100
I came here to congratulate your
intellect.

73
00:12:38,340 --> 00:12:39,660
Tell me, Helen!

74
00:12:41,200 --> 00:12:46,320
Osman took the bait you threw at him.

75
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:48,120
Perfect!

76
00:12:48,220 --> 00:12:52,920
Today I learned Aniton and his daughter
were the ones who helped Osman flee.

77
00:12:52,980 --> 00:12:55,320
Let's tell him to cook for us.

78
00:12:56,160 --> 00:13:02,660
And her daughter shall serve wine so
that I can kill them together.

79
00:13:24,520 --> 00:13:26,040
Osman.

80
00:16:09,660 --> 00:16:11,200
Brother!

81
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,100
Take my brother away!

82
00:17:24,099 --> 00:17:25,859
Careful!

83
00:18:57,340 --> 00:18:58,780
Ya Allah!

84
00:19:04,640 --> 00:19:06,060
Draw your swords!

85
00:19:16,720 --> 00:19:17,840
Alps!

86
00:19:18,300 --> 00:19:20,020
Fall back!

87
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:27,160
Damn it! Don't let him run away!

88
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:08,520
Osman!

89
00:20:12,520 --> 00:20:13,820
Let's go!

90
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:21,340
Osman!

91
00:20:23,200 --> 00:20:25,970
You won't escape from me this time!

92
00:22:00,980 --> 00:22:02,100
Ya Allah!

93
00:22:09,280 --> 00:22:10,780
Ya Allah!

94
00:23:35,160 --> 00:23:36,520
This...

95
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:40,140
... is for my brother.

96
00:24:07,580 --> 00:24:09,080
Brother.

97
00:24:22,340 --> 00:24:24,120
Brother!

98
00:24:25,800 --> 00:24:27,120
I'm okay.

99
00:24:27,320 --> 00:24:29,980
He is okay and he will get better,
insallah.

100
00:24:34,060 --> 00:24:35,480
Osman!

101
00:24:36,180 --> 00:24:38,600
I'm going to finish you, Osman!

102
00:24:39,460 --> 00:24:43,440
One day I'm going to catch you and
finish you off!

103
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:47,020
Alps! We are going to Tent.

104
00:24:47,280 --> 00:24:49,380
-Come on!
-As you order, my Bey.

105
00:24:49,780 --> 00:24:50,940
Brother.

106
00:25:03,760 --> 00:25:05,100
Aniton.

107
00:25:06,040 --> 00:25:08,460
Where is your daughter, Eftelya?

108
00:25:13,040 --> 00:25:15,280
Where is Eftelya?

109
00:25:20,980 --> 00:25:22,860
So you don't understand?

110
00:25:26,220 --> 00:25:31,780
I'm going to kill you and your daughter,
Aniton.

111
00:26:13,960 --> 00:26:15,540
Traitor dog!

112
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:17,720
You dog!

113
00:26:22,380 --> 00:26:25,200
Your daughter is going to die
just like you.

114
00:26:25,220 --> 00:26:26,780
Traitor!

115
00:27:09,440 --> 00:27:11,040
They know everything.

116
00:27:11,320 --> 00:27:12,940
This is your last chance.

117
00:27:48,640 --> 00:27:50,880
You little devil.

118
00:27:53,360 --> 00:27:56,900
You will no longer play tricks on us.

119
00:28:07,480 --> 00:28:10,860
If there is something better than
killing a Turk...

120
00:28:11,980 --> 00:28:15,360
... I'm pretty sure it must be killing
a traitor.

121
00:28:17,240 --> 00:28:18,880
I'm going to kill you!

122
00:28:19,380 --> 00:28:21,060
Don't worry.

123
00:28:21,820 --> 00:28:23,380
You are next.

124
00:28:26,260 --> 00:28:27,860
Take him.

125
00:28:39,240 --> 00:28:40,580
Move!

126
00:29:05,880 --> 00:29:08,920
Hold on, brother. Hold on.

127
00:29:16,620 --> 00:29:18,080
Faster!

128
00:29:19,100 --> 00:29:21,060
We are almost there.

129
00:29:21,220 --> 00:29:22,700
Faster!

130
00:29:23,500 --> 00:29:25,080
To the Tent of healing!

131
00:29:25,460 --> 00:29:27,400
Open the way!

132
00:29:35,800 --> 00:29:37,440
Savcı!

133
00:29:45,140 --> 00:29:46,520
Come on, faster!

134
00:29:47,800 --> 00:29:49,000
Move aside!

135
00:29:49,140 --> 00:29:50,620
Please, be strong.

136
00:29:50,720 --> 00:29:53,420
Stop!

137
00:29:57,100 --> 00:29:58,620
My Savcı.

138
00:30:01,120 --> 00:30:02,320
Savcı!

139
00:30:03,340 --> 00:30:05,760
My Savcı! Who did this to you?

140
00:30:06,580 --> 00:30:08,820
Who could do such a thing to you?

141
00:30:10,780 --> 00:30:12,980
Please say something!

142
00:30:14,080 --> 00:30:16,480
I'm begging you, please!

143
00:30:17,740 --> 00:30:19,960
We need to check his wound.

144
00:30:21,960 --> 00:30:24,720
Open your eyes, Savcı!

145
00:30:24,940 --> 00:30:27,780
-Aunt.
-Take your hands off me!

146
00:30:30,780 --> 00:30:32,680
Where is my son, Osman Bey?

147
00:30:34,300 --> 00:30:37,300
You made a promise! Where is he?

148
00:30:41,060 --> 00:30:44,420
Not only my son but also my bey, you took
from me.

149
00:30:44,800 --> 00:30:46,500
Shame on you.

150
00:30:47,360 --> 00:30:49,100
Shame on you!

151
00:30:55,860 --> 00:30:58,220
Open your eyes, Savcı!

152
00:30:59,880 --> 00:31:03,320
Please, I'm begging you. Open your
eyes!

153
00:31:08,420 --> 00:31:09,880
Savcı!

154
00:31:10,080 --> 00:31:11,420
Come on!

155
00:31:23,220 --> 00:31:27,020
Eftelya has just died too, Nikola.

156
00:31:28,440 --> 00:31:33,000
Do you hear, young man? Someone else
died because of you again.

157
00:31:33,180 --> 00:31:36,080
I'm going to drown you in your own blood.

158
00:31:44,620 --> 00:31:46,240
What a pity.

159
00:31:47,080 --> 00:31:49,420
His father said the same thing.

160
00:31:50,440 --> 00:31:52,220
What happened to him?

161
00:31:54,680 --> 00:31:56,120
What happened?

162
00:31:56,140 --> 00:31:57,680
Do you want to know?

163
00:32:00,220 --> 00:32:04,540
Flatyos stabbed him in the guts just
like this.

164
00:32:06,460 --> 00:32:09,500
A hard death he will go through
I suppose.

165
00:32:10,600 --> 00:32:13,600
You are lying!

166
00:32:15,740 --> 00:32:21,960
Flatyos, can you please tell us what we
accomplished thanks to this young man?

167
00:32:29,020 --> 00:32:33,180
We caught all the spies in our castle
thanks to him, Nikola.

168
00:32:34,440 --> 00:32:37,060
Yes. What else?

169
00:32:37,800 --> 00:32:43,060
And in exchange of his live, we will
get Kulacahisar back.

170
00:32:45,120 --> 00:32:46,960
Do you hear?

171
00:32:48,100 --> 00:32:52,800
Do you think my uncle Osman will leave
you unpunished?

172
00:32:53,980 --> 00:32:56,800
Enough about your uncle already!

173
00:32:56,980 --> 00:32:59,140
Man up a little bit.

174
00:32:59,660 --> 00:33:03,900
Whatever had happened, happened
because of you!

175
00:33:04,020 --> 00:33:10,900
The son of Ertuğrul Gazi, Savcı Bey, died
because of his stupid son!

176
00:33:11,660 --> 00:33:13,340
You are lying.

177
00:33:13,660 --> 00:33:15,620
Prepare to...

178
00:33:28,740 --> 00:33:31,540
You will regret not killing me
already.

179
00:33:37,160 --> 00:33:38,960
Stand him up.

180
00:33:45,520 --> 00:33:49,380
Are you going to be my killer?

181
00:34:11,620 --> 00:34:17,340
Listen to me carefully, young man.
Your uncle, Osman...

182
00:34:17,340 --> 00:34:21,620
... in exchange of your life, he is going
to give back Kulacahisar...

183
00:34:21,760 --> 00:34:27,620
... willingly and without having
second thoughts, to me.

184
00:34:27,800 --> 00:34:32,800
-No!
-Yes!

185
00:34:33,719 --> 00:34:35,719
Take him away.

186
00:34:40,679 --> 00:34:42,080
Father!

187
00:34:44,500 --> 00:34:49,300
-Please don't leave me, Savcı!
-Lena, step back!

188
00:34:50,060 --> 00:34:51,719
Lena!

189
00:34:51,800 --> 00:34:55,480
Please open your eyes, Savcı!

190
00:34:55,840 --> 00:34:58,680
-Lena, stop.
-Here it is, Bala Hatun.

191
00:34:58,840 --> 00:35:00,410
Don't touch me!

192
00:35:02,484 --> 00:35:04,464
Get off!

193
00:35:05,153 --> 00:35:06,833
Oh, Osman Bey!

194
00:35:06,833 --> 00:35:10,983
Osman Bey! Oh, Osman Bey!

195
00:35:10,983 --> 00:35:14,983
Your brother! Your brother!

196
00:35:14,983 --> 00:35:19,543
How will you build your state
over your brother's body?

197
00:35:19,543 --> 00:35:23,543
Enough, my girl!
Get off!

198
00:35:23,543 --> 00:35:27,543
Come on! Come on!

199
00:35:29,331 --> 00:35:33,331
How will you sit on that throne,
Osman Bey?

200
00:35:33,331 --> 00:35:37,331
Hold on, my lion.
Hold on.

201
00:35:37,331 --> 00:35:42,281
How will you sit on that throne,
Osman Bey?

202
00:35:42,521 --> 00:35:46,521
Hold on, my lion.
Hurry, girls!

203
00:35:46,521 --> 00:35:50,521
What are you waiting for?
Come on!

204
00:35:50,877 --> 00:35:53,127
Give it to me.

205
00:35:54,106 --> 00:35:56,636
Here it is.

206
00:35:57,096 --> 00:36:00,716
Hold on, brother.
Hold on.

207
00:36:01,120 --> 00:36:03,660
His wounds are heavy.

208
00:36:04,619 --> 00:36:08,619
We should fire it.

209
00:36:09,210 --> 00:36:14,280
Boil some water, women!

210
00:36:17,461 --> 00:36:22,601
Hold on, my lion. Hold on!
He has a fever!

211
00:36:22,601 --> 00:36:26,601
Hurry, I say! Hurry!

212
00:36:26,795 --> 00:36:31,695
Prepare the ember!
Bring it!

213
00:36:31,984 --> 00:36:37,164
Get off! Get off! Bring that here!

214
00:36:37,475 --> 00:36:41,475
He will be healed!
He will be healed!

215
00:36:45,475 --> 00:36:50,585
I won't leave you!
I won't leave you!

216
00:36:50,708 --> 00:36:53,558
Boil some water!

217
00:36:54,277 --> 00:36:58,277
Don't let yourself go!

218
00:36:59,730 --> 00:37:02,000
Brother...

219
00:37:09,345 --> 00:37:13,345
Now, everyone saw that
Osman lost.

220
00:37:13,345 --> 00:37:17,345
The rest will be easier.

221
00:37:18,582 --> 00:37:22,582
Everyone loses, woman.

222
00:37:22,582 --> 00:37:27,362
But a bey with many enemies
shouldn't lose.

223
00:37:27,999 --> 00:37:33,119
Then, he'll be crushed under
his tent.

224
00:38:01,091 --> 00:38:05,091
-Salam Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam.

225
00:38:08,320 --> 00:38:12,320
Nikola played us through our
spies in the castle.

226
00:38:12,320 --> 00:38:17,320
He hit us on our hearts.
I wish...

227
00:38:20,205 --> 00:38:23,285
...I hadn't listened to my brother.

228
00:38:24,430 --> 00:38:27,100
I felt it.

229
00:38:28,885 --> 00:38:34,585
I felt it.
I felt it.

230
00:38:35,315 --> 00:38:39,315
His pain for his child,
made me weak.

231
00:38:39,380 --> 00:38:44,620
In such times, instead of the enemy...

232
00:38:45,229 --> 00:38:50,669
...your love hurt you.

233
00:38:51,975 --> 00:38:55,975
We'll get over this as well.

234
00:38:56,928 --> 00:39:01,818
With Allah's will, we'll get up.

235
00:40:19,364 --> 00:40:21,734
Bayhoca.

236
00:40:33,098 --> 00:40:36,058
No...

237
00:40:41,527 --> 00:40:46,357
My bey, we found this.

238
00:40:58,495 --> 00:41:02,495
If you don't leave Kulucahisar
tomorrow...

239
00:41:04,029 --> 00:41:08,029
...like your spies...

240
00:41:09,767 --> 00:41:13,767
...the owner of this armor will die.

241
00:41:22,547 --> 00:41:26,547
Gather the beys at once.

242
00:41:27,734 --> 00:41:32,184
Bayhoca or Kulucahisar.

243
00:41:32,859 --> 00:41:36,859
Now is the time to decide.

244
00:42:06,553 --> 00:42:12,473
Shame on you, Osman Bey.
You lost my son to the enemy.

245
00:42:12,473 --> 00:42:17,663
And you used my husband as a bait.
Shame on you.

246
00:42:21,420 --> 00:42:26,290
Your pain will end soon.

247
00:42:38,390 --> 00:42:42,390
But the pain in my heart.

248
00:42:42,390 --> 00:42:44,570
The pain in your heart.

249
00:42:47,196 --> 00:42:51,196
-Be patient, Savcı.
-Lena.

250
00:42:51,622 --> 00:42:56,442
Hazal Hatun, you see that I'm busy.
Leave.

251
00:42:59,605 --> 00:43:03,605
I wouldn't come here if...

252
00:43:03,605 --> 00:43:06,925
...the news didn't concern you.

253
00:43:10,193 --> 00:43:14,753
Osman Bey's spy in Kulucahisar is
killed.

254
00:43:18,944 --> 00:43:24,484
And Bayhoca...
How can I say...

255
00:43:27,193 --> 00:43:29,323
Speak!

256
00:43:31,056 --> 00:43:36,826
That heathen Nikola!
He sent Bayhoca's armor...

257
00:43:37,785 --> 00:43:42,555
...and says that he will kill him
if we don't leave Kurucahisar.

258
00:43:50,082 --> 00:43:54,852
No... No...
No...

259
00:44:05,614 --> 00:44:10,654
My son... Please, my son...

260
00:44:11,858 --> 00:44:15,858
Savcı... Please, my son...

261
00:44:23,866 --> 00:44:28,656
No... No...
No...

262
00:44:29,258 --> 00:44:33,258
My son... No...

263
00:44:41,591 --> 00:44:48,301
With Allah's ninety-nine names...

264
00:44:49,514 --> 00:44:54,134
...who creates everything and
fills our hearts with faith.

265
00:45:01,060 --> 00:45:05,060
You all know the matter.

266
00:45:05,060 --> 00:45:10,390
The heathen Nikola wants
Kulucahisar Castle...

267
00:45:12,210 --> 00:45:15,770
...in return for my nephew Bayhoca.

268
00:45:17,427 --> 00:45:22,877
I want to talk to you before
making the decision.

269
00:45:24,357 --> 00:45:27,157
Bamsı Bey.

270
00:45:30,457 --> 00:45:35,417
Kulucahisar Castle was conquered
with the price...

271
00:45:35,417 --> 00:45:40,119
...of many lives and blood
from our martyrs.

272
00:45:42,402 --> 00:45:46,402
I swore with my alps
in that castle...

273
00:45:46,402 --> 00:45:50,402
...to never leave that castle
without a fight.

274
00:45:52,002 --> 00:45:58,142
Now, I can't tell those lions...

275
00:45:58,308 --> 00:46:03,878
...that we'll leave without a fight.
I won't.

276
00:46:06,235 --> 00:46:10,235
So, Osman Bey...

277
00:46:10,357 --> 00:46:14,357
...I don't want to leave
the castle.

278
00:46:23,677 --> 00:46:29,487
-Brother.
-He is my nephew...

279
00:46:30,227 --> 00:46:36,917
...but it's about a Kayı bey
rather than a nephew.

280
00:46:42,107 --> 00:46:47,957
It hurts to leave him to the heathens,
I know.

281
00:46:48,226 --> 00:46:52,226
We can't do anything, I know that too.

282
00:46:56,836 --> 00:47:01,576
I'll give up on my life to save him.

283
00:47:01,576 --> 00:47:05,576
But, Osman Bey, you know it too...

284
00:47:06,881 --> 00:47:10,881
...our lands are sacred.

285
00:47:11,451 --> 00:47:15,451
They can't be left for anyone's
favor.

286
00:47:19,309 --> 00:47:23,309
What do you say, uncle?

287
00:47:23,864 --> 00:47:27,864
-What do you say?
-Bayhoca...

288
00:47:28,842 --> 00:47:32,842
...is like my grandson.

289
00:47:32,842 --> 00:47:36,842
But even for him...

290
00:47:36,842 --> 00:47:40,842
...we can't leave the castle.

291
00:47:40,842 --> 00:47:45,042
We shouldn't even think about that.

292
00:47:48,680 --> 00:47:55,080
The bey has Allah's blessing.
He has the wisdom.

293
00:47:56,191 --> 00:48:00,191
He makes the best decision.

294
00:48:01,777 --> 00:48:05,777
I'm sure that he'll make the right
decision.

295
00:48:12,069 --> 00:48:16,069
A castle can be retaken.

296
00:48:16,069 --> 00:48:20,069
But we can't revive a life lost.

297
00:48:20,069 --> 00:48:24,069
We can't leave Bayhoca to the heathen.
We should leave the castle.

298
00:48:24,069 --> 00:48:28,069
And get Bayhoca.
And this way...

299
00:48:28,069 --> 00:48:30,309
...the war will be over.

300
00:48:43,960 --> 00:48:46,110
We will...

301
00:48:49,050 --> 00:48:51,660
...leave Kulucahisar.

302
00:49:15,599 --> 00:49:18,309
Forgive me, Savcı.

303
00:49:20,789 --> 00:49:24,789
I loved you at first sight.

304
00:49:25,722 --> 00:49:29,722
I will love you until my
last breath.

305
00:49:31,722 --> 00:49:37,202
If it's time for separation,
it doesn't fit us to rebel, you said.

306
00:49:38,775 --> 00:49:43,615
But a mother's heart can't
take it.

307
00:49:45,931 --> 00:49:49,361
I'm going to our son, Savcı.

308
00:49:49,903 --> 00:49:53,903
If they try to kill our child...

309
00:49:53,903 --> 00:49:58,693
...I want to protect him.

310
00:50:00,776 --> 00:50:04,826
I want to see his eyes
for the last time.

311
00:50:04,826 --> 00:50:07,476
That's all I can.

312
00:50:08,791 --> 00:50:13,161
I know how much you care
about your honor.

313
00:50:14,323 --> 00:50:21,213
Don't worry, I rather kill myself
than harm your honor.

314
00:50:23,693 --> 00:50:26,193
Savcı...

315
00:50:26,902 --> 00:50:32,792
...my valiant, give me your blessing.

316
00:50:44,332 --> 00:50:49,682
Castles can get conquered.
Enemies can get defeated.

317
00:50:50,283 --> 00:50:54,283
Lost provinces can get retaken.

318
00:50:54,504 --> 00:50:59,484
But it's not easy to raise
a Kayı bey.

319
00:51:00,233 --> 00:51:05,543
A Kayı bey can't be left
to the enemy.

320
00:51:07,482 --> 00:51:11,802
For this reason, I'll get my
nephew back...

321
00:51:13,096 --> 00:51:17,096
...and leave the castle.
That's my decision.

322
00:51:22,027 --> 00:51:26,677
Osman Bey, am I hearing wrong?

323
00:51:26,893 --> 00:51:30,893
Or are you leaving Kulucahisar?

324
00:51:31,896 --> 00:51:37,026
You heard it right, Bamsı Bey.
I'm leaving Kulucahisar.

325
00:51:38,548 --> 00:51:42,548
No, no. Osman Bey I know...

326
00:51:42,548 --> 00:51:46,708
...Osman Bey I know can't say that.

327
00:51:46,961 --> 00:51:51,831
-He wouldn't say that.
-You don't know me well then, Bamsı Bey.

328
00:51:56,042 --> 00:52:02,922
Uncle. Go to the heathen Nikola.
Tell him that we are leaving the castle.

329
00:52:29,667 --> 00:52:32,157
May I enter?

330
00:52:35,685 --> 00:52:37,585
My bey.

331
00:52:42,510 --> 00:52:45,130
My bey.

332
00:52:45,367 --> 00:52:48,037
Come, Baysungur.

333
00:52:51,957 --> 00:52:54,867
Lena?

334
00:52:54,867 --> 00:52:58,197
-Where is Lena?
-I don't know, my bey.

335
00:52:58,197 --> 00:53:00,747
I haven't seen her.
I brought you ointment.

336
00:53:23,965 --> 00:53:26,317
Lena?

337
00:53:26,601 --> 00:53:31,647
Lena, no... No...
You can't go to that castle.

338
00:53:32,156 --> 00:53:34,751
Baysungur!

339
00:53:34,751 --> 00:53:37,751
Help me.

340
00:53:38,869 --> 00:53:43,979
Help me. I need to talk to Osman.

341
00:53:53,464 --> 00:53:56,854
I need to see Osman Bey.

342
00:54:01,303 --> 00:54:05,303
Osman Bey!
Osman Bey!

343
00:54:05,303 --> 00:54:09,743
Leaving a conquered castle is against
our traditions.

344
00:54:09,743 --> 00:54:13,743
Even the bey can't step over the
traditions.

345
00:54:13,743 --> 00:54:18,023
On this matter, Osman Bey,
I warn you.

346
00:54:18,023 --> 00:54:23,703
The decision is made. There is no
reason to talk any longer.

347
00:54:24,112 --> 00:54:28,962
It's my decision.

348
00:54:32,164 --> 00:54:36,824
You wouldn't go against the traditions
if it wasn't your nephew.

349
00:54:36,986 --> 00:54:40,986
You are right, Bamsı Bey.
He is my nephew.

350
00:54:40,986 --> 00:54:43,866
And I want him here,
safe and sound.

351
00:54:44,025 --> 00:54:48,025
Osman Bey!
Osman Bey!

352
00:54:48,025 --> 00:54:52,025
I didn't live this long to see our
traditions disrespected!

353
00:54:52,025 --> 00:54:58,185
If you will step over it,
you must step over me first!

354
00:55:07,520 --> 00:55:10,480
Osman Bey.

355
00:55:11,783 --> 00:55:14,943
Bamsı Bey.

356
00:55:15,370 --> 00:55:22,100
What are you saying?
The future of Kayı...

357
00:55:22,862 --> 00:55:29,052
...doesn't depend on that decision
or this attitude. Calm down.

358
00:55:33,092 --> 00:55:38,852
We've talked and said everything.

359
00:55:39,843 --> 00:55:46,053
Now, we'll get Bayhoca and
leave Kulucahisar.

360
00:55:46,299 --> 00:55:48,629
This is my decision.

361
00:55:51,926 --> 00:55:55,926
Osman Bey...
Osman Bey!

362
00:55:58,230 --> 00:56:01,420
Lena went to the castle, brother.

363
00:56:01,420 --> 00:56:05,420
Brother!
Brother!

364
00:56:06,323 --> 00:56:10,323
Don't worry.

365
00:56:10,323 --> 00:56:14,323
I will save both Bayhoca
and Lena.

366
00:56:22,233 --> 00:56:27,533
Come on, Baysungur.
Take my brother to his tent.

367
00:56:38,512 --> 00:56:42,512
Everyone except Bamsı Bey will
leave.

368
00:57:57,578 --> 00:58:00,318
Lena.

369
00:59:08,160 --> 00:59:12,160
I've waited for you to come
for years.

370
00:59:13,799 --> 00:59:17,219
But you came for your son.

371
00:59:18,220 --> 00:59:23,370
Flatyos, is my son all right?

372
00:59:25,442 --> 00:59:29,442
-Where is Bayhoca?
-If you hadn't married that Turk...

373
00:59:30,427 --> 00:59:34,427
...he would be our son.

374
00:59:38,819 --> 00:59:41,879
Flatyos...

375
00:59:42,789 --> 00:59:49,579
...show me my son, let me see
that he is all right. I ask nothing else.

376
00:59:52,260 --> 00:59:57,060
For the woman who chooses a Turk
over me...

377
01:00:00,098 --> 01:00:04,098
...why should I do such a thing, Lena?

378
01:00:06,352 --> 01:00:10,352
I'll beg you if you like.

379
01:00:11,771 --> 01:00:15,771
I'll kneel befor you.

380
01:00:16,510 --> 01:00:20,510
There is nothing I can't do for my child.

381
01:00:22,461 --> 01:00:27,671
For Jesus Christ's sake, Flatyos.

382
01:00:28,890 --> 01:00:32,890
Let me see my child.

383
01:00:33,253 --> 01:00:35,823
Please.

384
01:00:53,108 --> 01:00:57,898
Oh, brother, oh.
I thought wrong.

385
01:00:58,668 --> 01:01:02,668
You are leaving the castle
for my child.

386
01:01:04,695 --> 01:01:09,975
You faced us all to conquer
that castle.

387
01:01:10,395 --> 01:01:15,765
Now you are facing everyone to
leave it. How can I repay you?

388
01:01:20,151 --> 01:01:24,151
You have my blessing, brother.

389
01:01:30,288 --> 01:01:34,288
But how can a conquered castle
be left?

390
01:01:34,532 --> 01:01:39,352
It's against our traditions.
Don't.

391
01:01:39,730 --> 01:01:43,730
Even for my child, don't.

392
01:01:43,878 --> 01:01:48,868
You'll lose your power,
your supporters.

393
01:01:49,011 --> 01:01:51,341
Don't.

394
01:01:52,141 --> 01:01:57,651
My dear brother,
my dearest brother.

395
01:01:58,585 --> 01:02:03,555
As long as you support me...

396
01:02:04,561 --> 01:02:08,561
...I don't need anyone else.

397
01:02:09,310 --> 01:02:12,270
Thank you, brother.

398
01:02:14,419 --> 01:02:22,199
I'm wounded. You know, I can't do
anything. We've brought you trouble.

399
01:02:24,299 --> 01:02:26,919
You weren't conscious, brother.

400
01:02:26,919 --> 01:02:33,069
How could you know?
Don't worry, I'll save them both.

401
01:02:34,624 --> 01:02:37,584
Whatever the price.

402
01:02:39,895 --> 01:02:42,479
Brother...

403
01:02:43,254 --> 01:02:45,326
...the castle...

404
01:02:46,963 --> 01:02:49,572
Brother?

405
01:02:55,432 --> 01:02:57,719
Brother?

406
01:03:42,785 --> 01:03:46,125
-Mother?
-Bayhoca!

407
01:03:47,375 --> 01:03:51,515
What are you doing here?
Have they captured you?

408
01:03:51,515 --> 01:03:55,515
What have they done to you?

409
01:03:58,158 --> 01:04:00,378
Are you hurt?

410
01:04:00,537 --> 01:04:02,537
No...
No...

411
01:04:07,725 --> 01:04:14,125
My child, how could they hurt you...

412
01:04:15,186 --> 01:04:21,976
Mother? Are you not a captive?
What are you doing here?

413
01:04:24,109 --> 01:04:28,109
My father?
How is my father?

414
01:04:30,111 --> 01:04:36,671
-This is enough, Lena.
-Mother, do you know this dog?

415
01:04:39,503 --> 01:04:43,503
Why is he treating you well?

416
01:04:46,328 --> 01:04:50,328
My son...
Bayhoca...

417
01:04:53,637 --> 01:04:57,637
I'll save you from here.
Don't worry.

418
01:05:01,692 --> 01:05:05,692
This is enough.
Soldiers.

419
01:05:06,019 --> 01:05:10,019
Flatyos, a little more, please.

420
01:05:10,019 --> 01:05:11,569
Lena.

421
01:05:19,411 --> 01:05:25,001
Where are you taking my mother?
Mother! Mother! Mother!

422
01:05:25,001 --> 01:05:27,051
Let my son go, Flatyos.

423
01:05:28,329 --> 01:05:31,739
Your son will die, Lena.

424
01:05:31,739 --> 01:05:34,389
He shouldn't have entered this castle.

425
01:05:40,000 --> 01:05:45,240
Flatyos. Let my son go.

426
01:05:45,442 --> 01:05:48,372
Take me as a captive.

427
01:05:48,372 --> 01:05:50,692
Taking you?

428
01:05:59,183 --> 01:06:03,683
Lena, there are only two
things that I want.

429
01:06:03,683 --> 01:06:08,233
The first is taking revenge
from my father's murderer.

430
01:06:12,298 --> 01:06:17,568
The second is seeing you as
my wife, Lena.

431
01:06:23,894 --> 01:06:28,594
In return for your son's life...

432
01:06:28,594 --> 01:06:30,944
...I want you to...

433
01:06:32,489 --> 01:06:36,489
...live here, in this castle
with me.

434
01:06:39,605 --> 01:06:42,485
Your son will return to his tribe.

435
01:06:44,251 --> 01:06:47,297
Stay with me here.

436
01:07:26,746 --> 01:07:30,746
I'm hearing right, Flatyos.
Am I not?

437
01:07:30,746 --> 01:07:35,956
You want me to release Savcı's son.
Is that so?

438
01:07:41,239 --> 01:07:45,239
Wouldn't you do this for me, Nikola?

439
01:07:46,174 --> 01:07:50,174
We'll release him and ambush him.

440
01:07:52,704 --> 01:07:56,704
Won't you do this for
your friend's love?

441
01:07:57,580 --> 01:08:02,190
The woman came all this way
to the castle, Flatyos.

442
01:08:02,667 --> 01:08:05,147
Be a man.

443
01:08:09,293 --> 01:08:13,293
What do you know about love, Nikola?

444
01:08:21,579 --> 01:08:25,579
Sir, Dündar Bey is here.

445
01:08:25,742 --> 01:08:30,232
This is good news.
Good news.

446
01:08:43,139 --> 01:08:45,989
Father.

447
01:08:52,536 --> 01:08:56,536
My ghazi father.

448
01:08:57,616 --> 01:09:01,616
My bey father.

449
01:09:06,418 --> 01:09:12,778
Who knows what
you've been through?

450
01:09:15,489 --> 01:09:19,489
How tough decisions
you had to take?

451
01:09:26,342 --> 01:09:31,192
Your beloved ones and
your people.

452
01:09:32,628 --> 01:09:37,908
Your family and your tribe.

453
01:09:39,581 --> 01:09:42,781
Your lands...

454
01:09:43,660 --> 01:09:49,920
...and your heart.
Your blood and your cause.

455
01:10:07,140 --> 01:10:12,760
This position is the place
of decisions.

456
01:10:15,463 --> 01:10:19,463
And it requires sacrifice.

457
01:10:24,454 --> 01:10:30,524
The people come before
your beloved ones.

458
01:10:32,375 --> 01:10:36,375
Your tribe is your family.

459
01:10:37,437 --> 01:10:43,237
Without lands,
there are no hearts.

460
01:10:44,351 --> 01:10:50,431
And our blood runs for
our cause.

461
01:10:57,928 --> 01:11:03,078
But I won't leave anyone.
Neither my sword...

462
01:11:04,245 --> 01:11:08,665
...nor my brothers,
nor...

463
01:11:10,903 --> 01:11:12,963
...my nephew.

464
01:11:18,288 --> 01:11:23,238
Dündar Bey, I'm tired of Osman.

465
01:11:24,667 --> 01:11:29,957
You should become the bey
as soon as possible.

466
01:11:41,282 --> 01:11:44,772
With the name of Allah.

467
01:11:52,552 --> 01:11:57,162
The Kayıs have a bey, Nikola.

468
01:11:57,688 --> 01:12:03,768
-And it's not easy to defeat him.
-That's why we are together, Dündar Bey.

469
01:12:03,833 --> 01:12:08,373
To help each other.

470
01:12:08,373 --> 01:12:13,133
So, your nephew Osman,
will he leave Kulucahisar?

471
01:12:13,827 --> 01:12:18,427
You know that he will, Nikola.

472
01:12:23,210 --> 01:12:29,050
-Where is Bayhoca?
-Flatyos, have them prepare Bayhoca.

473
01:12:29,725 --> 01:12:33,725
See, that was what you wanted.

474
01:12:48,952 --> 01:12:51,552
Dündar Bey.

475
01:12:51,823 --> 01:12:55,823
You are a step closer
to the throne.

476
01:12:57,211 --> 01:13:01,211
Because of me.

477
01:13:02,942 --> 01:13:06,422
Don't forget that.

478
01:13:07,580 --> 01:13:11,590
Thank you. Thank you.

479
01:13:12,003 --> 01:13:16,003
Don't doubt that.

480
01:13:23,761 --> 01:13:27,761
I beg you in Virgin Mary's name.

481
01:13:30,763 --> 01:13:34,763
Save my son.
Take me.

482
01:13:39,585 --> 01:13:43,585
Nikola accepted to release your
son, Lena.

483
01:13:45,261 --> 01:13:49,261
We'll pray for a new life now.

484
01:14:06,099 --> 01:14:10,099
-A new life.
-Yes, Lena.

485
01:14:12,589 --> 01:14:16,589
When will my son leave
the castle?

486
01:14:16,848 --> 01:14:20,848
He is about to leave, Lena.
Trust me.

487
01:14:50,898 --> 01:14:54,898
What are you doing?

488
01:14:55,469 --> 01:14:59,469
What are you doing, Lena?
Were you going to save your son...

489
01:14:59,469 --> 01:15:03,469
...and kill yourself? Were you going to
save your son and kill yourself, Lena?

490
01:15:03,844 --> 01:15:09,964
I told you before. Savcı is my
first and last love.

491
01:15:10,404 --> 01:15:14,404
He will remain that until my
last breath.

492
01:15:14,611 --> 01:15:18,611
Release my son and
take my life.

493
01:15:18,817 --> 01:15:20,837
That's all I can give.

494
01:15:51,937 --> 01:15:56,487
Osman accepted to give Kulucahisar
Castle for your son, Lena.

495
01:16:03,755 --> 01:16:07,755
Dündar Bey came to get your son.

496
01:16:08,343 --> 01:16:12,343
Thank God!

497
01:16:12,803 --> 01:16:16,803
Thank God for this!

498
01:16:19,315 --> 01:16:23,315
-Thank God!
-Soldiers!

499
01:16:24,836 --> 01:16:29,156
Take her. We'll reunite her
with her son.

500
01:16:29,156 --> 01:16:30,996
Thank God!

501
01:16:53,331 --> 01:16:58,191
Brother, will we give
that castle now?

502
01:16:58,810 --> 01:17:02,810
Tell me, Dumrul.
What should we do?

503
01:17:03,006 --> 01:17:06,456
Should we defy Osman Bey's orders?

504
01:17:11,543 --> 01:17:15,243
We lost many men
for that castle.

505
01:17:15,243 --> 01:17:18,233
I joined Osman Bey to conquer
castles, not give them.

506
01:17:18,838 --> 01:17:23,848
I know, Gencebey. I know.
I can't accept it either.

507
01:17:25,223 --> 01:17:29,223
Traditions on one side,
Osman Bey's order on the other.

508
01:17:30,677 --> 01:17:34,307
I'm helpless too, brother.

509
01:17:38,431 --> 01:17:42,431
Cerkutay, what are you doing there?

510
01:17:43,392 --> 01:17:47,392
Bamsı Bey taught me that alps
don't ask questions.

511
01:17:47,392 --> 01:17:50,662
So, I'm doing archery training.

512
01:17:55,900 --> 01:17:59,900
Aygül Hatun, don't you have
a thing to say?

513
01:18:08,048 --> 01:18:12,048
For me, Osman Bey is
the laws and the bey.

514
01:18:16,701 --> 01:18:20,701
This sword is under his command.

515
01:18:20,701 --> 01:18:25,551
If he says, swing,
I swing. If not, I'll forget it.

516
01:18:29,274 --> 01:18:33,274
Not only Kulucahisar, even if
he gives Söğüt with it...

517
01:18:33,274 --> 01:18:35,764
...I won't say a word.

518
01:18:52,606 --> 01:18:57,116
-Salam Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam.

519
01:19:03,248 --> 01:19:07,248
-Any wounded?
-No, my bey.

520
01:19:21,613 --> 01:19:27,383
My bey, Nikola accepted it.
They'll give Bayhoca.

521
01:19:27,589 --> 01:19:31,589
-Thank Allah.
-Thank Allah.

522
01:19:33,349 --> 01:19:36,309
Thank Allah.

523
01:19:36,411 --> 01:19:40,411
My bey, will we really give
the castle?

524
01:19:53,900 --> 01:19:59,830
Mother, tell me. How do you know
Flatyos?

525
01:20:02,357 --> 01:20:06,927
Thank God, we left that castle.
There is no need to think that.

526
01:20:06,927 --> 01:20:10,927
Mother, how do you know Flatyos?

527
01:20:30,181 --> 01:20:33,241
Turks are leaving the castle.

528
01:20:33,834 --> 01:20:37,834
-What about the christians?
-None are left, sir.

529
01:20:38,240 --> 01:20:41,560
Good news.

530
01:20:43,233 --> 01:20:47,233
Alexander, search the castle.

531
01:20:47,233 --> 01:20:52,013
Dündar Bey's companion will
come with you.

532
01:20:53,730 --> 01:20:57,730
No living creature will be left
in the castle.

533
01:20:57,730 --> 01:21:02,000
Kill everything that moves.

534
01:21:02,428 --> 01:21:06,428
I'll wait for your news.

535
01:21:19,791 --> 01:21:25,501
-Are you afraid that Osman might act up?
-I'm taking measures.

536
01:21:26,600 --> 01:21:32,210
Otherwise, I will burn them alive.

537
01:21:33,424 --> 01:21:37,424
You will die as well, Dündar Bey.

538
01:21:37,737 --> 01:21:41,737
I know. I know.

539
01:21:42,438 --> 01:21:46,438
-I know.
-Pray that...

540
01:21:48,475 --> 01:21:52,475
...your nephew won't make a mistake.

541
01:22:57,230 --> 01:23:01,790
The castle is empty. Here is our flag.

542
01:23:09,519 --> 01:23:15,049
Now, Dündar Bey will bring Bayhoca
and Lena Hatun.

543
01:23:36,482 --> 01:23:41,582
If anything goes wrong...

544
01:23:41,582 --> 01:23:43,682
...slit their throats.

545
01:24:25,930 --> 01:24:28,890
Search everywhere!

546
01:24:43,285 --> 01:24:46,705
Check the secret passage!

547
01:25:01,141 --> 01:25:04,111
Sir, it's empty.

548
01:25:10,052 --> 01:25:13,462
Sir, the secret passage is empty.

549
01:25:54,291 --> 01:25:58,291
Has Osman Bey kept his word?

550
01:25:58,291 --> 01:26:00,731
Easy victories scare me.

551
01:26:05,365 --> 01:26:10,765
We searched everywhere. There was
no one but two drunkards. We killed them.

552
01:26:11,118 --> 01:26:15,118
Go and tell Flatyos that the castle
is ours.

553
01:26:15,422 --> 01:26:18,782
-And give him the escrow.
-Yes, commander.

554
01:26:18,782 --> 01:26:24,842
Long live Nikola!
Long live Alexander!

555
01:26:25,281 --> 01:26:29,281
Get to the walls!

556
01:26:59,744 --> 01:27:02,324
The castle is secure.

557
01:27:02,324 --> 01:27:08,744
Long live Nikola!
Long live Alexander!

558
01:27:58,722 --> 01:28:01,962
The castle is clear, sir.

559
01:28:07,049 --> 01:28:09,329
Dündar Bey.

560
01:28:10,942 --> 01:28:16,332
Thanks to them, we are having
a bloodless victory.

561
01:28:16,332 --> 01:28:20,332
And by the way, it's that easy
to defeat Osman Bey.

562
01:28:40,656 --> 01:28:45,306
Now, I'm the ruler of here.

563
01:28:45,306 --> 01:28:49,306
It's the oath of the lord of Kulucahisar
Alexander.

564
01:28:49,306 --> 01:28:55,306
Karacahisar and Söğüt are next in line.
I will end the Kayı!

565
01:28:55,411 --> 01:29:01,381
Long live Nikola!
Long live Alexander!

566
01:29:06,456 --> 01:29:12,276
Don't, son. Don't.

567
01:29:12,276 --> 01:29:16,276
Who has more reason to cry, mother?

568
01:29:16,276 --> 01:29:20,856
Because of me, Osman Bey
left Kulucahisar Castle.

569
01:30:01,037 --> 01:30:05,957
How can I look at Osman Bey?
How can I look at the people, uncle?

570
01:30:06,365 --> 01:30:11,135
We left the castle that was taken
with blood, because of me!

571
01:30:12,249 --> 01:30:17,369
This shame is ours together, Bayhoca.

572
01:30:17,369 --> 01:30:22,169
The ones who caused this should
be ashamed.

573
01:30:23,534 --> 01:30:28,844
In time, everything will be done.

574
01:30:31,143 --> 01:30:35,143
I thought Osman Bey had an iron will,
Dündar Bey.

575
01:30:35,143 --> 01:30:39,143
But he is softhearted enough to
give us a castle for this idiot.

576
01:30:42,522 --> 01:30:46,522
Bayhoca! Bayhoca!

577
01:30:46,522 --> 01:30:50,972
Get out of here before I change my
mind and hang you.

578
01:30:51,583 --> 01:30:56,553
Come on. Come on, let's go.

579
01:30:57,398 --> 01:31:01,398
Mother, I can't live with this shame.

580
01:31:02,938 --> 01:31:06,938
Come on, son. Let's go.

581
01:31:38,040 --> 01:31:42,340
Osman gave the castle but he'll
do everything to take it back.

582
01:31:42,340 --> 01:31:46,340
With the supply we brought, we can
defend it for months.

583
01:31:46,498 --> 01:31:50,718
Osman doesn't have a single spy.
He can't enter the castle.

584
01:31:50,718 --> 01:31:55,138
-He has to siege Kulucahisar.
-Isn't this what we want?

585
01:31:55,138 --> 01:32:00,438
He should so that we can crush the
Turks inside and out with Nikola.

586
01:32:06,220 --> 01:32:11,150
-What are you doing here, woman?
-I'm hanging clothes, don't you see?

587
01:32:11,150 --> 01:32:15,460
Dresses of my children,
my stupid husband's clothes...

588
01:32:15,460 --> 01:32:21,320
A woman's job never ends.
Don't you have anything to do?

589
01:32:32,550 --> 01:32:37,790
We missed you. We missed you,
Abdurrahman Ghazi. We missed you.

590
01:32:37,790 --> 01:32:42,810
You disappeared suddenly.
But you did a great job.

591
01:32:42,810 --> 01:32:48,560
-So, alps are ready for a mission, huh?
-We missed you too.

592
01:32:49,069 --> 01:32:53,069
That's what Osman Bey ordered.
He wanted me to...

593
01:32:53,069 --> 01:32:57,069
...form a death squad which will
hunt...

594
01:32:57,069 --> 01:33:01,069
...Geyhatu's commanders.

595
01:33:01,069 --> 01:33:05,069
Thank Allah, that's what we did.

596
01:33:05,069 --> 01:33:07,659
Mashallah. Mashallah.

597
01:33:09,069 --> 01:33:14,539
Arslan Bey, Osman Bey invites you
to Kulucahisar.

598
01:33:14,539 --> 01:33:18,129
He invites you to his jihad.

599
01:33:18,129 --> 01:33:23,039
It's a must for a Muslim to accept
an invite for jihad.

600
01:33:23,039 --> 01:33:28,289
Of course, we will come.
But tell me, Bamsı Bey...

601
01:33:28,289 --> 01:33:32,289
...did you believe that Osman Bey
would give the castle?

602
01:33:33,815 --> 01:33:39,905
Good question, Arslan Bey.
Back in time...

603
01:33:40,012 --> 01:33:45,392
...when Ertuğrul Ghazi did things that
we couldn't understand, we believed in him.

604
01:33:45,909 --> 01:33:49,909
Now we do the same for
Osman Bey.

605
01:33:56,347 --> 01:34:00,347
Attack, my valiants!

606
01:34:16,606 --> 01:34:20,606
-Ya Allah!
-For Allah!

607
01:34:21,864 --> 01:34:25,864
It's not enough to put soldiers
on the walls.

608
01:34:25,864 --> 01:34:29,864
We also need hot oil.

609
01:34:29,864 --> 01:34:32,284
On north--

610
01:34:32,991 --> 01:34:38,401
-Turks are in the castle, they are attacking!
-God damn it! How could that happen?

611
01:34:52,261 --> 01:34:56,261
Osman!

612
01:35:02,070 --> 01:35:06,070
Alps! In our tradition...

613
01:35:06,070 --> 01:35:10,420
...can we leave a conquered castle?

614
01:35:10,597 --> 01:35:16,657
-No, my bey.
-Can a bey step over the traditions?

615
01:35:16,909 --> 01:35:22,089
-No, my bey.
-That's what I'm saying.

616
01:35:22,614 --> 01:35:27,444
A conquered castle can never be
given back.

617
01:35:27,444 --> 01:35:33,364
-The traditions can't be stepped over.
-Won't we save Bayhoca, my bey?

618
01:35:33,364 --> 01:35:37,364
We'll save Bayhoca.

619
01:35:37,364 --> 01:35:41,364
And Kulucahisar will be their
graveyard.

620
01:35:41,845 --> 01:35:45,845
Come on! What are you waiting for?

621
01:35:45,845 --> 01:35:49,845
-It's time for jihad.
-All right, my bey.

622
01:36:27,898 --> 01:36:31,048
Catch them!

623
01:37:00,270 --> 01:37:05,000
Ayaz, Gencebay!

624
01:37:05,092 --> 01:37:09,432
-Swing your swords for Allah!
-Attack, my lions! Allahu Akbar!

625
01:37:09,435 --> 01:37:13,435
Allahu Akbar!

626
01:37:25,533 --> 01:37:31,133
I will kill you this time, Osman.
I swear that I will.

627
01:37:32,273 --> 01:37:37,715
I will give you my life,
as I gave you the castle.

628
01:37:39,180 --> 01:37:44,320
Come and keep your oath.

629
01:38:34,550 --> 01:38:37,940
What are you doing here, mad girl?

630
01:38:37,940 --> 01:38:42,550
I'm doing what you are doing,
mad lad. I'm fighting for the Kayı.

631
01:38:45,167 --> 01:38:49,167
You may get hurt.

632
01:38:49,167 --> 01:38:53,167
-Mind your business!
-This is my business!

633
01:38:53,431 --> 01:38:57,431
Osman Bey is in the castle.
Hurry!

634
01:38:58,550 --> 01:39:03,920
-May Allah bless your hands.
-Stop talking and run to the castle.

635
01:39:04,232 --> 01:39:07,512
Lead the way.

636
01:39:59,660 --> 01:40:01,980
Now.

637
01:40:03,594 --> 01:40:07,594
Keep your oath.

638
01:40:07,888 --> 01:40:11,888
This is your last chance...

639
01:40:11,888 --> 01:40:15,398
...to kill me.

640
01:40:21,461 --> 01:40:25,461
Your corpse will leave my castle, Osman.

641
01:40:25,461 --> 01:40:29,461
I will raid your tribe and
kill everyone.

642
01:41:11,483 --> 01:41:14,421
-Osman Bey!
-Osman Bey!

643
01:41:25,387 --> 01:41:28,607
Before dying...

644
01:41:35,964 --> 01:41:38,764
...I want you to know.

645
01:41:39,512 --> 01:41:46,232
Ask for their saddles from Turks,
and they will.

646
01:41:47,464 --> 01:41:52,464
Ask for their horses,
and they will.

647
01:41:53,027 --> 01:41:58,117
When you are in tough times,
they will give you their bread.

648
01:41:59,094 --> 01:42:03,734
When they are trapped,
they will give their lives.

649
01:42:04,509 --> 01:42:07,079
But...

650
01:42:08,845 --> 01:42:14,005
...even a crumble of soil that
was washed with blood...

651
01:42:15,070 --> 01:42:20,670
...can never be given
without a fight.

652
01:42:25,251 --> 01:42:30,681
When weasels set a trap,
wolves bleed.

653
01:42:30,816 --> 01:42:37,456
But when wolves set a trap,
all weasels die.

654
01:43:03,932 --> 01:43:09,222
Now, I have my nephew...

655
01:43:11,717 --> 01:43:15,377
...and the castle.

656
01:43:24,908 --> 01:43:29,388
Osman Bey, now we have the castle.

657
01:43:29,388 --> 01:43:33,388
Thank you.
Thank you.

658
01:43:33,678 --> 01:43:37,678
Dündar Bey took Lena and
Bayhoca to the tribe.

659
01:43:37,912 --> 01:43:42,972
My bey, let's reach to the tribe
before Bayhoca runs out of tears.

660
01:43:44,188 --> 01:43:48,188
Now, he is ready to be an alp.

661
01:43:51,939 --> 01:43:55,939
Boran, send Alexander...

662
01:43:55,939 --> 01:43:59,939
...to his owner's door.

663
01:43:59,939 --> 01:44:03,939
We should send a gift back.

664
01:44:05,292 --> 01:44:09,292
As you order, my bey.

665
01:44:57,841 --> 01:45:03,051
Osman Bey leaves Kulucahisar for
his nephew. May Allah help us.

666
01:45:21,511 --> 01:45:25,511
What's wrong, Aksu Hatun?
What are you doing here?

667
01:45:25,511 --> 01:45:29,511
-I came to save you from your thoughts.
-What thought?

668
01:45:34,174 --> 01:45:38,174
I heard that our bey is a captive.

669
01:45:42,727 --> 01:45:47,997
True. Kayı beys are thinking for a
way to save him.

670
01:45:47,997 --> 01:45:51,047
You came for nothing.

671
01:45:51,806 --> 01:45:57,856
Forgive me for acting over my level.
If you allow me.

672
01:45:58,974 --> 01:46:04,694
My daughter, come. Sit.

673
01:46:04,800 --> 01:46:09,830
Tell us how to be saved from
our thoughts.

674
01:46:20,591 --> 01:46:25,141
May Allah bless us.
I saw a dream last night.

675
01:46:25,141 --> 01:46:27,651
I hope it's good.

676
01:46:28,818 --> 01:46:34,008
There was a baby. Crying
in flames.

677
01:46:34,021 --> 01:46:39,251
A woman was crying to save
that baby.

678
01:46:40,626 --> 01:46:44,626
Then, a wolf showed up,
jumped into the flames.

679
01:46:46,171 --> 01:46:52,461
The baby mounted the wolf, got out
of the flames and reunited with his mother.

680
01:46:58,645 --> 01:47:02,645
The baby is Bayhoca.

681
01:47:02,907 --> 01:47:06,167
He will reunite with his mother.

682
01:47:08,140 --> 01:47:12,410
-Inshallah.
-Inshallah.

683
01:47:15,860 --> 01:47:20,410
-Inshallah.
-I will return to Söğüt.

684
01:47:20,887 --> 01:47:24,887
If you need something, tell me.

685
01:47:26,922 --> 01:47:32,792
Stay here, Aksu Hatun.
I need you.

686
01:47:59,025 --> 01:48:03,025
I've been waiting for this
for a long time.

687
01:48:03,624 --> 01:48:08,194
Interesting enough, it was easy.

688
01:48:08,918 --> 01:48:12,918
Let's take over our castle.

689
01:48:12,918 --> 01:48:14,568
Yes.

690
01:48:24,326 --> 01:48:27,366
Helen?

691
01:48:29,080 --> 01:48:35,080
Dear Helen,
without losing a single soldier...

692
01:48:35,540 --> 01:48:39,540
...a single soldier,
we took that castle!

693
01:48:39,978 --> 01:48:45,388
-Nikola.
-Why did you dress like this?

694
01:48:45,668 --> 01:48:48,878
Why do you look like a crow
in our victory day?

695
01:48:48,878 --> 01:48:50,668
Nikola.

696
01:48:57,105 --> 01:49:02,555
Helen?
Is something wrong?

697
01:49:04,949 --> 01:49:08,949
-Osman...
-So, Helen? Osman?

698
01:49:12,178 --> 01:49:15,108
Soldiers!

699
01:49:44,158 --> 01:49:48,158
What's in the box, Helen?

700
01:50:11,548 --> 01:50:14,748
Alexander...

701
01:50:20,902 --> 01:50:24,902
My friend...

702
01:50:42,723 --> 01:50:47,653
Osman...
Osman!

703
01:50:52,825 --> 01:50:56,105
Burn it.

704
01:51:10,707 --> 01:51:17,297
Ashes to ashes...
... dust to dust.

705
01:51:22,993 --> 01:51:27,353
Your God has already left us, Petrus.

706
01:51:30,089 --> 01:51:38,270
May God forgive your sins.

707
01:51:39,239 --> 01:51:41,599
The God?

708
01:51:43,515 --> 01:51:47,845
I never worshipped your God
for my empire.

709
01:51:48,069 --> 01:51:52,069
But I might worship the devil
from now, Petrus.

710
01:51:52,069 --> 01:51:56,069
You will tell me everything now!

711
01:51:56,791 --> 01:52:00,471
First, what do you want from Osman?

712
01:52:00,471 --> 01:52:04,291
Second, what do you want to
take from him?

713
01:52:04,463 --> 01:52:09,253
No games, no lies.
You will tell me everything.

714
01:52:09,483 --> 01:52:13,483
Tell me before sending you to devil.

715
01:52:28,509 --> 01:52:34,219
Since you understood that the path
to God goes from the devil...

716
01:52:35,112 --> 01:52:40,352
...you deserve to learn the truth,
Nikola.

717
01:52:43,568 --> 01:52:47,568
The future of the Turks...

718
01:52:47,568 --> 01:52:51,568
...is in Osman's tent.

719
01:52:54,866 --> 01:52:58,866
To stop the Turks...

720
01:52:58,866 --> 01:53:02,866
...to take their future from them...

721
01:53:02,866 --> 01:53:08,546
...it's time for that great war.

722
01:53:09,800 --> 01:53:15,600
-What does that mean?
-To unite the tribes...

723
01:53:15,636 --> 01:53:19,636
...Osman has that great power.

724
01:53:20,111 --> 01:53:25,621
And if does that,
it will be your doom first...

725
01:53:27,154 --> 01:53:32,594
...then it will be our doom, Nikola.

726
01:53:34,235 --> 01:53:40,635
When Kayı Tribe is in chaos,
we'll enter Osman's tent...

727
01:53:40,635 --> 01:53:44,635
...and get the documents.

728
01:53:45,687 --> 01:53:49,687
Bamsı will open the door...

729
01:53:49,687 --> 01:53:52,597
...for his tent.

730
01:53:56,916 --> 01:54:01,826
İdris Bey, İdris Bey!
Why are you chasing me?

731
01:54:01,921 --> 01:54:04,911
What medicine is this?

732
01:54:04,911 --> 01:54:10,481
It's healing, Bamsı Bey. I've been
searching for this since I saw your hand.

733
01:54:10,525 --> 01:54:15,965
Sit, sit. Will this help me?

734
01:54:15,965 --> 01:54:19,965
Yes, will you die if
you try it?

735
01:54:19,965 --> 01:54:23,965
If it heals, you will fight
with two swords as you used to before.

736
01:54:28,930 --> 01:54:32,490
Give it to me.

737
01:54:41,229 --> 01:54:45,919
-Will I put it in my hand?
-Yes, on your hand.

738
01:54:47,639 --> 01:54:51,639
Like this.

739
01:55:12,800 --> 01:55:17,630
-What's this, sir?
-You'll give it to Bamsı.

740
01:55:17,630 --> 01:55:20,490
It will heal his hand.

741
01:55:20,913 --> 01:55:25,183
It will be so good that he will
ask for more.

742
01:55:25,183 --> 01:55:30,343
As he wants more,
we'll give him more.

743
01:55:32,742 --> 01:55:37,372
We should spread it like this so
it can heal you.

744
01:55:39,151 --> 01:55:44,351
We'll see, İdris Bey.
We'll see.

745
01:55:57,754 --> 01:56:01,754
Move!

746
01:56:06,207 --> 01:56:11,077
Sargun Bey!
Merciless leader of the Cumans!

747
01:56:11,077 --> 01:56:15,077
I brought you Lord Nikola's regards!

748
01:56:32,509 --> 01:56:36,509
I brought you gold.

749
01:56:40,828 --> 01:56:46,808
A lot of gold for the most
merciless warriors I've ever seen.

750
01:56:51,585 --> 01:56:59,175
I came to give gold to those who
came for it.

751
01:57:10,348 --> 01:57:14,082
I came to rain gold on you.

752
01:57:16,204 --> 01:57:20,135
Sargun Bey!
This is the beginning!

753
01:57:38,476 --> 01:57:40,690
Targun Hatun!

754
01:57:55,958 --> 01:58:02,508
-Göktuğ?
-I came to end our deal, Flatyos.

755
01:58:26,034 --> 01:58:30,034
Göktuğ and I killed Sargun...

756
01:58:30,034 --> 01:58:34,034
...who took my father's throne.

757
01:58:34,647 --> 01:58:39,797
From now, I'm leading the Cumans.

758
01:58:45,580 --> 01:58:49,580
So, you came to take revenge,
Targun Hatun?

759
01:58:49,713 --> 01:58:54,413
Yes, for revenge.

760
01:58:54,760 --> 01:59:00,920
In a most bloody way. In most
cruel way.

761
01:59:02,425 --> 01:59:06,425
The gold we'll get from Nikola...

762
01:59:06,425 --> 01:59:10,425
...the spoils we'll get from Turkish
lands...

763
01:59:10,425 --> 01:59:15,835
...but most importantly,
the revenge we'll get from Osman.

764
01:59:24,744 --> 01:59:31,094
-Are you following me?
-You don't know where to go.

765
01:59:31,414 --> 01:59:36,514
Just because Osman Bey sent me
away, I'm not homeless.

766
01:59:36,514 --> 01:59:42,564
-I know where to go.
-You are right. You have a tribe to go.

767
01:59:43,686 --> 01:59:48,506
I left the Mongols for Osman Bey.
Now I have nowhere to go.

768
01:59:49,329 --> 01:59:53,329
What will you do now?

769
01:59:54,864 --> 02:00:01,744
I'll make living by my sword.
Someone will need me.

770
02:00:08,432 --> 02:00:12,432
I came for a new agreement.

771
02:00:12,780 --> 02:00:17,620
But, don't forget.

772
02:00:17,748 --> 02:00:22,338
I haven't forgotten anything yet.

773
02:00:37,650 --> 02:00:42,260
Dodurğa, Bayat, Salur Tribes...

774
02:00:42,518 --> 02:00:46,518
...they are spread everywhere.

775
02:00:46,518 --> 02:00:50,518
Mongols left no unity.

776
02:00:51,295 --> 02:00:56,175
We need to unite them,
for a new cause.

777
02:00:56,231 --> 02:01:00,861
For new goals,
we need to unite them.

778
02:01:02,909 --> 02:01:06,909
These escrows,
my ancestors...

779
02:01:06,909 --> 02:01:11,549
...shout ''Are you still
waiting, Osman?''

780
02:01:13,949 --> 02:01:16,619
They ask where our state is.

781
02:01:19,209 --> 02:01:25,609
All tribes will come together.
I'll give them a home.

782
02:01:25,875 --> 02:01:31,065
I'll give them lands,
goals.

783
02:01:32,348 --> 02:01:36,348
I'll build an army.

784
02:01:36,348 --> 02:01:41,288
And I will kick the heathens
out of these lands.

785
02:01:45,139 --> 02:01:49,139
I promised you, father.

786
02:01:49,139 --> 02:01:53,139
I will keep my word.

787
02:02:06,029 --> 02:02:10,029
Oh, my son. Oh...

788
02:02:14,969 --> 02:02:20,859
Bayhoca, when your father comes,
whatever he says...

789
02:02:21,281 --> 02:02:24,701
...don't say a thing.

790
02:02:25,469 --> 02:02:31,209
-Do you get it?
-He will come at you because of me.

791
02:03:08,346 --> 02:03:12,346
How can you do this?

792
02:03:12,888 --> 02:03:15,888
How?

793
02:03:16,748 --> 02:03:21,538
Father, I made a mistake but--

794
02:03:24,039 --> 02:03:27,259
Bayhoca...

795
02:03:27,351 --> 02:03:30,021
But?

796
02:03:31,560 --> 02:03:34,370
But?

797
02:03:35,070 --> 02:03:39,070
But people died because of you!

798
02:03:39,407 --> 02:03:43,687
-People!
-Savcı Bey!

799
02:03:48,602 --> 02:03:52,602
You destroyed my honor!

800
02:03:54,296 --> 02:03:58,296
How can you go to that castle
without telling me?

801
02:03:58,437 --> 02:04:01,687
How?

802
02:04:04,815 --> 02:04:07,455
Also...

803
02:04:10,150 --> 02:04:14,150
...with a child on your belly...

804
02:04:22,140 --> 02:04:26,140
Hit me, Savcı Bey.
Go on.

805
02:04:26,320 --> 02:04:31,240
Hit to a mother who is
in pain for her child.

806
02:04:32,912 --> 02:04:38,372
My Allah, you are the one who
gives patience to us.

807
02:04:39,162 --> 02:04:45,442
Woman, we live for our honor,
don't you know that?

808
02:04:46,510 --> 02:04:50,510
We'll die if needed.
But...

809
02:04:57,005 --> 02:05:01,005
Are you ashamed? Huh?

810
02:05:01,379 --> 02:05:07,049
Tell me, are you ashamed?
Your mother begged to the enemy!

811
02:05:07,049 --> 02:05:09,409
Are you ashamed?

812
02:05:18,651 --> 02:05:25,281
I am ashamed, father.
I'm ashamed for causing all this.

813
02:05:32,545 --> 02:05:37,485
Be ashamed.
Be ashamed.

814
02:05:41,643 --> 02:05:45,643
You too.

815
02:05:47,723 --> 02:05:53,323
From now, if you do anything
without telling me...

816
02:05:54,354 --> 02:05:58,354
...I will kill you both with
my own hands.

817
02:06:07,052 --> 02:06:11,052
-Father?
-Savcı!

818
02:06:11,052 --> 02:06:13,752
-Father!
-Savcı!

819
02:06:13,843 --> 02:06:19,303
-Father, are you all right?
-Savcı, are you all right?

820
02:06:20,674 --> 02:06:23,414
I'm fine.

821
02:06:30,616 --> 02:06:34,136
I'm fine.

822
02:06:40,642 --> 02:06:44,242
He came and ruined everything.

823
02:06:44,242 --> 02:06:48,642
He played us all by saying
he will give the castle.

824
02:06:48,642 --> 02:06:53,362
While we were talking about
it in the tent...

825
02:06:53,362 --> 02:06:57,362
...he set his game already.

826
02:07:05,114 --> 02:07:10,844
Woman, leave that and say something.

827
02:07:11,669 --> 02:07:16,169
I'm waiting for you to calm down,
Dündar Bey.

828
02:07:16,530 --> 02:07:20,830
Last time, when you were
choking me...

829
02:07:21,164 --> 02:07:25,684
...you said something.

830
02:07:26,575 --> 02:07:30,575
What did you say?

831
02:07:30,575 --> 02:07:34,575
Don't push an angry man!

832
02:07:39,383 --> 02:07:42,893
Was that what you said?

833
02:07:42,893 --> 02:07:47,573
Yeah, I said.

834
02:07:47,573 --> 02:07:52,003
But I didn't tell you to not
speak a word.

835
02:08:09,451 --> 02:08:13,451
Do you know why Osman
succeeds...

836
02:08:13,451 --> 02:08:17,451
...and you do not?

837
02:08:17,627 --> 02:08:21,627
Yes, tell me. Tell me.

838
02:08:23,660 --> 02:08:29,370
When Osman builds a plan,
he trusts in himself.

839
02:08:30,170 --> 02:08:34,170
But you trust in others.

840
02:08:37,616 --> 02:08:41,616
Should I be silent or leave?

841
02:08:44,026 --> 02:08:49,206
What should I do? Huh?
What should I do?

842
02:08:50,840 --> 02:08:54,840
Build your own plan...

843
02:08:54,950 --> 02:08:58,950
...and don't trust anyone.

844
02:09:04,618 --> 02:09:08,618
You are right.

845
02:09:26,193 --> 02:09:29,573
In Bayhoca Matter...

846
02:09:31,031 --> 02:09:35,031
...we are guilty...

847
02:09:35,031 --> 02:09:39,391
...after all, we kept him away
from the tribe.

848
02:09:40,472 --> 02:09:45,552
We wanted him to
know science...

849
02:09:45,570 --> 02:09:49,570
...learn trade.

850
02:09:49,612 --> 02:09:53,612
These are surely important.

851
02:09:54,262 --> 02:09:58,262
But for a Kayı bey...

852
02:09:58,262 --> 02:10:02,262
...responsibility is the most important.

853
02:10:04,947 --> 02:10:10,627
A Kayı bey should know...

854
02:10:11,201 --> 02:10:16,761
...that the price is heavy,
when he makes a mistake.

855
02:10:19,404 --> 02:10:24,964
You can't learn it from a school,
but from experience.

856
02:10:27,916 --> 02:10:31,916
You are right, brother.
But...

857
02:10:32,002 --> 02:10:36,002
...we sent them to not
suffer as we did...

858
02:10:36,002 --> 02:10:40,002
...to get good education.

859
02:10:40,114 --> 02:10:45,134
I know, brother. I know.
That's what I'm saying.

860
02:10:46,670 --> 02:10:51,640
Our children shouldn't go away.

861
02:10:51,773 --> 02:10:55,773
Science shouldn't
be away from us.

862
02:10:55,982 --> 02:11:01,292
It should be here.
Teachers should come here.

863
02:11:02,536 --> 02:11:09,146
Firstly, we should be students.

864
02:11:09,408 --> 02:11:13,408
Then, we should teach.

865
02:11:15,595 --> 02:11:21,445
Inshallah, brother.
I don't know if we'll see those days.

866
02:11:21,848 --> 02:11:25,848
-But inshallah, they will.
-Inshallah.

867
02:11:27,425 --> 02:11:32,705
They will, brother. They will.
I wish we could too.

868
02:11:33,205 --> 02:11:37,995
But, a three doesn't grow in one day.

869
02:11:42,900 --> 02:11:45,910
And you, Bayhoca...

870
02:11:46,536 --> 02:11:52,166
...you owe me now.
You won't act on your own.

871
02:11:53,956 --> 02:11:57,956
When I say jihad,
you'll go to jihad.

872
02:11:58,135 --> 02:12:02,135
When I say sit,
you'll sit.

873
02:12:03,579 --> 02:12:09,839
If you don't listen to me,
if you make your parents sad again...

874
02:12:10,465 --> 02:12:15,815
...then, you'll see my fury.

875
02:12:16,198 --> 02:12:20,198
I got my lesson, Osman Bey.

876
02:12:21,275 --> 02:12:25,275
From now, I will listen to my mother...

877
02:12:25,275 --> 02:12:29,275
...to my father
and to you.

878
02:12:32,610 --> 02:12:36,170
May I enter, my bey?

879
02:12:36,367 --> 02:12:38,537
Come.

880
02:12:43,082 --> 02:12:48,282
-My bey, Kumrul Abdal wants to come.
-Let him come.

881
02:13:01,468 --> 02:13:05,468
Why are you sitting like this?

882
02:13:07,005 --> 02:13:12,035
-Someone is coming, Osman Bey!
-Who is that?

883
02:13:12,388 --> 02:13:16,388
One who solves all mysteries...

884
02:13:16,388 --> 02:13:20,388
...one who has a throne in our hearts,
sultan of Ahis, Sheikh Edebali!

885
02:13:21,568 --> 02:13:25,568
Father!

886
02:13:44,096 --> 02:13:47,606
My Sheikh, Edebali.

887
02:13:53,920 --> 02:14:04,170
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com